Chapter: EffectMapEffctx
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils

 Acceptance probe (effect rows stage 0). An effectful function
 mapped inside a def that DECLARES [Console], with the effectful
 result act-bound before use. Under effect rows this is the
 row-polymorphic happy path (list-map's row variable instantiates to
 {Console}, which the signature covers) and must always compile and
 print. Guards stage 3 against over-rejection, and regression-tests
 CL 6508: the act-bound r must strip EffectfulTy through a resolved
 type variable, or list-length r trips CDX2031.

Section: Definitions

  shout : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  shout (n) = act
    print-line-uni ("shout " & show n)
    n * 2
  end

  mapper : List Integer -> [Console] (List Integer)
  mapper (xs) = list-map shout xs

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    r <- mapper [4, 5]
    print-line-uni ("len " & show (list-length r))
  end
